    "short_description": "FNB South Africa, or First National Bank, is the oldest bank in the country, founded in 1838 as the Eastern Province Bank. It operates as a division of FirstRand Bank Limited and is headquartered in Johannesburg. With over 7.2 million customers, FNB is one of the \"Big Four\" retail banks in South Africa, providing a wide range of banking services.\n\nThe bank offers personal, private, business, commercial, and corporate banking solutions. Its services include personal banking for individuals and families, tailored private banking for high-net-worth clients, and support for small to medium enterprises. FNB also provides wealth management, home finance, and commercial banking services for larger entities. The bank is committed to environmental responsibility and has initiatives focused on conservation and sustainability. Additionally, FNB has expanded its reach into Southern Africa, operating in countries like Botswana, Namibia, Mozambique, and Eswatini.",
